 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The sky is on her; she glides along,\nShe leads a swan in the water's tide;\nAnd she speaks, and sings to the ocean\nWith the song of the sunshine.\nThe river sends its laughter\nAcross the fields where it runs along,\nIts gurgling sound alone,\nIts flowing melody song\nOf wild womanhood that flies along.\nOut of the fields how she passes,\nBrow bowed, eyes closed, ear aflame,\nWhere the waters relax",
